{
  "input": "# 0005 \u2014 Add a waiting list when a meetup is full\n\n- Status: open\n- Labels: app/backend, feature\n- Found: 2026-09-16, a member asked to be notified when a full meetup frees a seat\n\n## Problem\n\nA meetup with `capacity` already reached refuses every further signup\nwith a flat 409. Members who wanted in have no way to be notified if a\nspot opens up later, so they give up and go elsewhere. We want a\nwaiting list: once a meetup is full, further signups join a queue\ninstead of being rejected outright, and when a confirmed attendee\ncancels, the first person on the queue takes their seat.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nGiven a meetup at capacity\nWhen a new member signs up\nThen they are added to the waiting list instead of getting a 409\n\nGiven a waiting list with at least one member\nWhen a confirmed attendee cancels their signup\nThen the first member on the waiting list is promoted to attendee\n\nGiven a member already on the waiting list\nWhen they sign up again for the same meetup\nThen the request is rejected as a duplicate, not queued twice",
